course: dictionary
lesson: 4438
title: Handler: a person who looks after or deals with things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A handler is a person who looks after, trains or deals with something. The word before handler tells you what they handle. «The call handler is trained to help even a frightened child.» A call handler answers calls for help, so the handler is the person who deals with the calls.
explain: «Police dogs are trained to follow a scent trail; when they retire they often live with their handler.» Here the handler trains and looks after the dog. You can check the meaning by swapping in your own idea: does "the person who looks after the dog" fit? It does, so you have understood the word.
explain: Handler can also mean a piece of computer code. «An event handler» is the code that runs when something happens, such as a click on a button. The same word works in all of these places, so look at the words around it to find the job it means.
fact: A handler is a person who trains, looks after, or deals with something.
fact: The word before handler tells you the job: «dog handler», «baggage handler», «food handler».
fact: A «baggage handler» moves bags and suitcases at an airport.
fact: A «food handler» deals with food, and must wash their hands.
fact: In computing, an «event handler» is the code that runs when something happens, like a click.
exercise: «The call handler is trained to help even a frightened child.» What is a call handler? | *A person who deals with emergency calls and helps the caller | A teacher who writes exam questions | A person who sells phones in a shop | A driver who takes children to school
exercise: «Police dogs ... when they retire they often live with their handler.» What is a handler here? | A police car with a siren | A dog that has stopped working | A kind of dog food | *The person who trains and looks after the dog
exercise: Ella's mum says, «The baggage handler found my lost suitcase.» What does a baggage handler do? | Sells tickets in a shop | *Moves and deals with bags at an airport | Cooks meals for passengers | Flies the plane
test: A coder writes «an event handler» that runs when you click a button. What does the handler do? | *Runs the code when the click happens | Sends a text message to a friend | Makes the button a new colour, every single time | Deletes the whole program
test: In «dog handler» and «food handler», what do the words before handler tell you? | The colour of the person's uniform | Nothing, they are just there to decorate the sentence | Their age and how tall they are | *The thing or animal the person looks after or deals with
exam: Which meaning of handler fits a person who guides and manages a famous singer? | A person who cooks food in a café | A person who trains horses only | *A person who guides and manages someone famous | A piece of computer code that runs when a click happens
